config T2_SIDECAR
	tristate "Apple T2 Sidecar video encoder support"
	depends on USB
	depends on MEDIA_SUPPORT && VIDEO_DEV
	select V4L2_MEM2MEM_DEV
	select VIDEOBUF2_VMALLOC
	help
	  Driver for the low-latency H.264/HEVC encoder the Apple T2 offers to
	  Sidecar. The T2 exposes it as a virtual USB device while t2remote
	  holds the com.apple.videoprocessingd.encode.remote connection. It is
	  exposed as a V4L2 memory-to-memory device.

	  If built as a module, it is called t2-sidecar.
